                "cve_id": "CVE-2023-34204",
                "title": "imapsync through 2.229 uses predictable paths under /tmp and /var ...",
                "description": "imapsync through 2.229 uses predictable paths under /tmp and /var/tmp in its default mode of operation. Both of these are typically world-writable, and thus (for example) an attacker can modify imapsync's cache and overwrite files belonging to the user who runs it.",
